  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Stephen Hawking is mapped as the sole exception to a rule",
  "description": "The text 'no one: steven hawking' is positioned above Stephen Hawking in the wheelchair, creating an analogical mapping where the text explicitly identifies him as the only person who cannot do something (presumably 'no one' can do it, but Hawking is the exception). This mapping is spatially and contextually anchored to his visual representation, projecting the textual claim directly onto him as the subject of the statement. The meme format 'no one: [Person]' is used to imply Hawking is the sole exception, which is a form of mocking disability and ableist stereotype.",
